; sandbox-determinism.t is gated-UPSTREAM (NEW-1, #18): its byte-stable
; profile_hash contract is blocked on an untracked upstream purity fix (make
; profile_hash a pure function of the sealed policy, not of a temp path) AND on
; the MENTAT_TEST_SANDBOX_CONFINED seam, neither of which has landed. It must not
; run — or false-green — on the default `blackbox` alias until then.
;
; Mechanism (same as the retired gated/ bucket): dune folds every matching cram
; stanza into one spec — aliases union, enabled_if accumulates and is ANDed. The
; parent whole-subtree stanza (test-cases/dune) attaches this .t to `blackbox`
; with no guard; this scoped stanza ANDs in the MENTAT_TEST_GATED guard, so the
; folded enabled_if is false unless MENTAT_TEST_GATED=1. No false green: the test
; simply does not run by default. The other sandbox/*.t are untouched — this
; stanza applies to sandbox-determinism alone. When the upstream fix lands, drop
; this file.

(cram
 (applies_to sandbox-determinism)
 (alias blackbox-gated)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{env:MENTAT_TEST_GATED=0} 1)))
